  "review": {
    "reviewer": "/root/golden_tests",
    "scope": "Independent read-only Rust benchmark, Python orchestration/offline validator and measurement contract review; copied-evidence Python controls only.",
    "no_remaining_blockers": true,
    "findings_resolved": [
      "Cargo configuration hashes were recorded but initially omitted from offline validation; final validation compares the complete current manifest.",
      "Initial allocation checks admitted inconsistent attempt counts; native code now proves omitted zero-size/zeroed/shrink operation categories are absent and the validator enforces attempts=allocate+grow.",
      "Coordinator independently strengthened cross-feature length/FNV comparison to saved complete frame bytes, with per-frame SHA/length/FNV binding.",
      "Normal and optimized controls both demonstrated JSON false accepted as exit code0; exact integer exit and string environment-value checks fix it."
    ],
    "reviewed_invariants": [
      "Three independent Python/Rust deterministic source recipes and nine reference parameter tuples.",
      "Source/request generation, allocation survey, whole-frame equality, decoding, frame saving and JSON formatting occur outside timed intervals.",
      "Global compression and returned output destruction remain inside each measured call.",
      "All configured executables are built before any run; ordered argv, effective environments, compiler/host and existing executable hashes are bound.",
      "Raw five-sample durations and iteration counts produce independently recomputed summaries only for explicitly timed campaigns.",
      "Exact source manifest and Cargo inputs are rechecked around every actual command."
    ],
    "limits": [
      "No timing measurements were run for this checkpoint; all samples are empty and all timing summaries null.",
      "Only safe and all-features smoke configurations have executed; 14-configuration timing is a later gated campaign.",
      "This review did not rerun compilation or codec checks. The coordinator performed all five smoke campaigns.",
      "Hashes verify saved artifacts, not authenticity against a malicious author; independent C interoperability has separate evidence.",
      "Historical smoke1 preset expectation correction was source-backed by pinned clevels.h80\u201381; original failure metadata/logs are retained."
    ],
